To increase structural durability without adding excessive weight, Tony constructed parts of the Mark XII using lightweight carbon-fiber composite materials alongside standard gold-titanium plating. The armor was designed to test high-speed stealth maneuvering, utilizing radar-absorbent body paneling and dampened repulsor thrusters. Though it never saw direct solo combat screen time prior to Iron Man 3, the Mark XII answered the House Party Protocol command, flying into the final battle before ultimately being destroyed in the "Clean Slate" detonation sequence.
